#: src/Import/MarkdownImportPage.php:114
msgid "How the import works"
msgstr ""

#: src/Import/MarkdownImportPage.php:115
msgid "Import Markdown into handbook pages. Paste a single draft or upload a ZIP of .md files: these become editable pages. If the ZIP contains a mkdocs.yml, its navigation defines the page structure, titles, and order (the ZIP must also hold the referenced files). Or give a GitHub URL: a file URL becomes one locked page, a folder (tree) URL imports every .md file in the folder as locked pages pulled from the repository. Front matter is dropped, transport metadata and the parent and order are applied, Mermaid diagrams and collapsible details become blocks, images in the ZIP are added to the media library, and internal .md links are pointed at the imported pages."
msgstr ""

